        topic: "Mixed",
        fp: "Defendant was walking down an alleyway behind an urban sports bar at midnight[cite: 55]. An intoxicated man carrying an unzipped canvas gym bag stumbled against Defendant, bumping Defendant's shoulder[cite: 55]. Defendant shoved the man away, causing the man to drop the gym bag onto the pavement[cite: 55]. Defendant looked down into the open bag and saw bundles of cash totaling $10,000[cite: 55]. Intending to keep the money permanently, Defendant reached down, picked up the gym bag, and placed the strap over his shoulder[cite: 55]. The man shouted, 'Hey, that's my money, give it back!', stepped forward, and grabbed Defendant's coat collar[cite: 55]. Defendant drew a heavy steel flashlight from his jacket, struck the man forcefully across the forehead, and knocked him unconscious to the pavement[cite: 55]. Defendant fled down the alley with the bag of cash[cite: 55]. The jurisdiction adheres to traditional common law property and theft offenses[cite: 55].",
